Finished the Layer 2 classifier spec. The key design decision was to pull the classification logic out into its own stateless interface (IScopeClassifier) rather than reusing IAgentVerifier — the semantics are different enough that mixing them would cause confusion. The idea is that a single deployed classifier contract can serve any number of markets; what gets committed at market creation is just the params (thresholds, sample requirements, aggregation method), not a new contract per market. Two reference implementations are covered — one for numeric/continuous data using MAD-based outlier filtering and median aggregation, one for categorical/enum data using plurality voting with a quorum threshold. Full spec in the gist https://gist.github.com/JimmyShi22/8ef5b25f928bea5e34df3f03fea03d67

